Package: syslinuxos-nvidia-setup
Version: 1.1.1
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: bash (>= 5), apt, coreutils, util-linux, yad, pkexec
Maintainer: Franco Conidi aka edmond <fconidi@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://syslinuxos.com
Description: NVIDIA driver setup with optional CUDA for SysLinuxOS and Debian
 Detect NVIDIA display adapters on SysLinuxOS 13 or Debian 13 amd64.
 Install compatible driver packages through APT.
 Includes a YAD frontend in the SysLinuxOS Tools menu and a terminal mode.
 Automatically selects English, Italian, Spanish, German or French.
 English is used for unsupported or unset system languages.
 CUDA Toolkit is optional. Secure Boot may require manual MOK enrollment.
 Installing this package does not install GPU drivers automatically:
 launch SysLinuxOS NVIDIA Setup to start the hardware-specific installation.
